# Running LVLme in Cursor

LVLme in Cursor should work but is not tested yet. If something does not
work, say so to the person plainly.

Follow `SKILL.md` in this folder exactly. It is the full procedure, and
`AGENTS.md` is the short version. Every script takes `--workspace PATH`.

1. Find the workspace: `$LVLME_HOME` (or the older `$CLIMB_HOME`), or the one
   folder in `~/lvlme-workspaces/` (or `~/climb-workspaces/` if only that
   older folder exists). For a new goal, follow "First run" in `SKILL.md`:
   `python3 scripts/init.py --goal "<goal>"`, then one short first message.
2. Run the ten stages in `SKILL.md`: intake (`method/INTERVIEW.md`), evidence,
   market, judge and audit (`method/RUBRIC.md`, `method/CONSISTENCY.md`,
   `method/RECRUITER_SCREEN.md`), review (`method/REVIEW.md`), score, SWOT and
   TOWS, plan and fixes (`method/PROFILE_FIXES.md`), report, tell the person.
3. If you can run tasks in parallel, fan out as
   `docs/ORCHESTRATION.md` describes, using the briefs in `agents/`.
   Otherwise run the stages one after another; the gates do not change.
4. The sceptical review and the recruiter screen must be independent: run
   them in a new chat, give that chat only the packet the procedure names,
   and paste its answer back. Never show it the campaign's scores.
5. Nothing is scored until every score above 2 has been reviewed.
6. Finish with a message under 150 words: the outlook, today's 1 to 3
   actions, what needs the person's answer or yes, and
   `open <workspace>/report/index.html`. The first time, also point them to
   the plain-English guide, `docs/for-you/READING-YOUR-DASHBOARD.md`.

For one part only, the person may ask for: quick (honest odds for one
posting from a link and a CV, in a couple of minutes: follow
`skills/lvlme-quick/SKILL.md`, and run its blind review in a new chat),
interview, audit, screen, dashboard, status, or resume (see "Entry points" in
`SKILL.md`).
